Not ported from Bitwarden (written for Kemlock): src/model.rs, context.rs, limits.rs, error.rs,
csv.rs (a Papa Parse-compatible reader), zip.rs, bwcrypto.rs (the KDF and EncString format of
password-protected exports, as Bitwarden's clients define them), passkey.rs, detect.rs, and
src/kdbx.rs (a wrapper over the keepass crate).

Dependencies with their own licences (all MIT or Apache-2.0 and checked by cargo-deny in CI):
  keepass 0.17 (MIT, sseemayer/keepass-rs), for KDBX 3.1 and 4.
  pgp 0.21 (rPGP; MIT or Apache-2.0), for Proton Pass's passphrase-encrypted exports.
  RustCrypto crates (aes, cbc, hmac, hkdf, sha2, argon2), miniz_oxide, base64, serde.

Bitwarden's source is read from the public repository; the fixtures under tests/fixtures are made
up for this crate and hold no real personal data.
